<h1>About tuaccesible</h1>

<div class="prose">
  <h2>María Pía Peña Foissac</h2>
  <img class="portrait" src="/img/maria-pia.jpg" width="1458" height="1534" alt="">
  <p>I've used NVDA as my screen reader for more than 13 years — it's my primary way of accessing digital content, both in daily life and at work. Since 2021 I've been doing manual, non-simulated accessibility audits of websites and mobile apps, evaluating the real barriers someone navigating with assistive technology runs into, not just what an automated tool flags. Beyond checking conformance, I look at whether an interface is genuinely usable for someone navigating that way.</p>
  <p>I also teach digital accessibility — at the DALAT Foundation and at XAcademy — which has sharpened how clearly I can explain technical barriers, to both technical and non-technical audiences.</p>

  <h2>Certifications</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A11Y Development Knowledge Badge — IAAP, January 2026.</li>
    <li>Digital Accessibility Specialist, WCAG 2.2 Level AA — Instituto de Accesibilidad, May 2025</li>
    <li>ARIA from Scratch for Developers and Designers — WeAAAre, July 2025</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>We work as a team</h2>
  <p>We're a team of accessibility professionals — every audit and every workshop is thought through and reviewed by more than one person, not in isolation.</p>
</div>
